# Artist Admin

One login for the studio — Sam and Rae each sign in with their own Google account to run the chair, the requests, and the deposits.
::

::form[submit="Sign in with Google"]
- Email (email) *
- Password (password) *
::

::callout[type=note title="Demo — login not wired up"]
On the live site this is one-tap Google sign-in, no separate password to manage. The dashboard below is what each artist sees after signing in.
::

::section
## The shared studio dashboard
::

::features[cols=3]
### Shared chair calendar

Both artists' personal Google Calendars sync in and overlay onto the one chair. If either calendar is busy, that window shows as taken — for both of them.

### No double-booking

Confirming a request checks both Google Calendars first — one conflict and it will not confirm. A clean confirm writes the session to both calendars and blocks the chair.

### Requests & deposits

Booking requests from the site and Instagram DMs land in one inbox. Confirm a time and the client gets a Square deposit link by text — paid means locked.
::

::infocard[title="How conflict-checking works"]
- **Connect once** — Sam and Rae each link their own Google Calendar the first time they sign in.
- **One chair, one truth** — the public chair calendar is a live overlay of both artists' busy times.
- **Confirm safely** — a request can only be confirmed into a window that is clear on both calendars; confirming writes the event to both and sends the Square deposit link.
::

